cc2400_test.c powers up the CC2400 wireless transceiver and exercises the SPI
control interface to verify that the CC2400 responds with an expected default
register value.

On success all LEDs are illuminated.

TX and RX blinking at about one hertz, with USR dark, means the radio answered
the SPI bus but never reported its reset register value. A radio that answers
nothing at all stops the test earlier, with TX and RX lit steadily.
